\title{Trace quality and productive persistence}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}
\tag{state}
\tag{harness}

\p{FTIP asks which parts of a long-horizon trace remain useful to a later
decision. The source horizon and selective-refinement observations are finite
conditional evidence, while the trace record, persistence predicates, and
build-repair example below make the retained events and state boundary
explicit \citet{Sections 3-7}{dang2026selecting}.}

\p{A useful horizon preserves the declared decision, evidence, verification,
and recovery events while separating repeatability from task and strategy
coverage. The fixed-budget protocol in \ref{ftip-00P3} supplies the finite
selection, receipt, and contrast definitions needed to test that distinction.}

